# hessboost vs XGBoost 3.4.1 on an Apple M3 Max (macOS 27.0, Rust
# 1.98.1, XGBoost PyPI wheel). Median of six fits per engine, from the
# 2026-09-26 run recorded in the tables in docs/performance.md, section
# 'XGBoost comparison'. Threads share dense f32 data, CPU hist, depth 6,
# 256 bins, 100 rounds. Chart source for docs/benchmarks/charts.gp.
#
# One row per workload, median fit seconds at 1, 4 and 16 threads
# (hessboost and XGBoost interleaved).
#
# label                seq_t1    xgb_t1    seq_t4    xgb_t4   seq_t16   xgb_t16
"Regression 100k × 30"      0.4120    1.0540    0.1579    0.3671    0.2029    0.3601
"Regression 50k × 128"      1.0571    3.2205    0.3566    0.9864    0.3263    0.6571
"Binary 100k × 30"          0.4021    1.0444    0.1562    0.3629    0.1991    0.3556
"4-class 50k × 30"          0.9289    2.5045    0.2987    0.9718    0.2353    1.1879
